Z||000000||bHooper||03-11-2001||11:05 PM||||is it true that you guys cant replace the front wheel bearings?  i understand that they cant be purchased new, any more.  <P>if they can, how expensive are they?  if not, what do you use?  what other parts are as difficult to obtain.<P>just curious.<BR><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000001||Black88GT||03-11-2001||11:17 PM||||Rodney Dickman has been working on this issue.  I believe the Fiero Store sells them but I am not sure.  Anywho, Rodney said we should see manufacturers start selling them in a couple months!  Thanks Rodney!<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fieropage/af.bmp"> ||||reg||14
Z||000002||Fformula88||03-11-2001||11:25 PM||||Hopefully Rodney can get some made up.  The Fiero Store has no more new ones as of January.  Otherwise, used ones will have to do the job.  When they were announced as discontinued I bought a pair of new ones and have been storing them since in anticipation of mine going bad.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||03-11-2001||11:32 PM||||I've been living with squeaking front wheel bearings for a year now.<P>Many '88 parts are special order. Calipers, rotors, ball-joints, tie-rod ends, most any suspension piece, brake pieces, steering racks, exhuast pieces, aluminum cooling tubes, a few engine sensors, etc. Not terrible, but if it's your only transportation, special orders can feel like an eternity. It's nice having a pre-'88 too, but the handling difference is night and day.||||reg||1
Z||000004||bHooper||03-12-2001||06:46 AM||||thanks for your good answers, fellas!  i was curious about this, not that i will be getting a '88 for a long time, but just interested to know the facts.<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000005||Alex4mula||03-12-2001||08:34 AM||||Oh s@&%^t! I have replaced three bearings on my Formula during its 13 years. The front driver's side is original and has 40K miles more than the last I replaced (car has 166K mi). I wonder when it will fail. Hope not soon...||||reg||1
